Containers and codecs for Hound streams. Hound proxies files as they are, and
torrent releases are almost always MKV -- but the stock configure-wiiu only
enables the mov, h264 and mp3 demuxers, so every MKV died in
avformat_open_input() with "Invalid data found" (-1094995529). This patch
enables the matroska demuxer (MKV/WebM/MKA), the AVI demuxer, and the audio
decoders those files usually carry (E-AC3, DTS, FLAC, Opus), plus the MP3
demuxer and parser from ffmpeg-wiiu-mp3-demuxer.patch (which this patch
supersedes -- either one alone is enough for MP3, both is fine too).

Video stays H.264 only: the console's decoder is h264_wiiu, so HEVC/x265
releases still refuse with "no decoder registered" -- pick an H.264 (x264)
release. An MKV whose audio can't be decoded now plays silently instead of
failing (see src/media/decoder.cpp).

--- a/configure-wiiu
+++ b/configure-wiiu
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 --disable-doc \
 --disable-everything \
---enable-decoder=mpeg4,h264_wiiu,aac,ac3,mp3 \
---enable-demuxer=mov,h264 \
+--enable-decoder=mpeg4,h264_wiiu,aac,ac3,mp3,eac3,dca,flac,opus \
+--enable-demuxer=mov,h264,mp3,matroska,avi \
 --enable-bsf=h264_mp4toannexb \
 --enable-filter=rotate,transpose \
 --enable-protocol=file \
